  "description": "The end of a period of months counted from a day, written as this example reads it: the day itself is not counted, the period ends on the day before the corresponding day of the last month, or on the last day of that month when it has no such day, and an end that falls on a day closed in England and Wales moves to the day after. It says nothing of how any law is read",
